From: enfs-dkms
Subject: [PATCH] include/linux/sunrpc/sched.h: widen tk_flags + add RPC_TASK_ENFS / RPC_TASK_FIXED

OpenEuler's enfs needs two new RPC_TASK_* flag bits on rpc_task:

  - RPC_TASK_ENFS  — task dispatched from the enfs subsystem
  - RPC_TASK_FIXED — task pinned to its current xprt by enfs path-monitor
                     / failover code (pm_ping.c, failover_path.c)

OE 6.6 used 0x0008 and 0x0040 respectively. **Neither is a free choice
in Ubuntu 7.0:**

  - 0x0008 happens to still be free in 7.0 (verified: only RPC_TASK_*
    flag missing from the full 0x0001–0x8000 enumeration in the stock
    file). RPC_TASK_ENFS gets that one.
  - 0x0040 is now `RPC_TASK_NETUNREACH_FATAL` in 7.0.
  - 0x0020 is `RPC_CALL_MAJORSEEN` (also stored in tk_flags).
  - 0x0100 is `RPC_TASK_NO_ROUND_ROBIN`.
  - Every other bit 0x0001–0x8000 in tk_flags is consumed.

So all 15 of the stock 16-bit positions are taken except the one we
claim for ENFS. RPC_TASK_FIXED has nowhere to go inside the original
`unsigned short` field.

**Fix:** widen `tk_flags` from `unsigned short` to `unsigned int`. The
lower 16 bits remain identical to stock (every stock define keeps its
value, every accessor macro keeps working), and we put RPC_TASK_FIXED
in the upper 16 (0x00010000) where no collision is possible. enfs
source uses both flags symbolically (verified `grep -rn 0x0040
fs/nfs/enfs/` returns nothing), so the bit-position change is
transparent to the OE code.

The struct grows by ≤ 4 bytes (often 0 after alignment). This changes
the symbol CRC of any sunrpc export whose signature mentions rpc_task,
which means nfsd.ko / lockd.ko / nfs_acl.ko built against stock
sched.h would refuse to load against our patched sunrpc.ko — but those
modules are already going to be rebuilt as part of the DKMS package
(see project task #17 / dkms.conf.in).

---
 include/linux/sunrpc/sched.h | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/include/linux/sunrpc/sched.h
+++ b/include/linux/sunrpc/sched.h
@@ -93,7 +93,7 @@ struct rpc_task {
 	int			tk_status;	/* result of last operation */
 	struct list_head	tk_task;	/* global list of tasks */

-	unsigned short		tk_flags;	/* misc flags */
+	unsigned int		tk_flags;	/* misc flags (widened by enfs to fit RPC_TASK_FIXED in upper 16) */
 	unsigned short		tk_timeouts;	/* maj timeouts */

 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SUNRPC_BACKCHANNEL)
@@ -144,6 +144,11 @@ struct rpc_task_setup {
 #define RPC_TASK_NO_RETRANS_TIMEOUT	0x4000		/* wait forever for a reply */
 #define RPC_TASK_CRED_NOREF	0x8000		/* No refcount on the credential */

+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_SUNRPC_ENFS)
+#define RPC_TASK_ENFS		0x00000008	/* enfs: dispatched by the enfs subsystem (matches OE) */
+#define RPC_TASK_FIXED		0x00010000	/* enfs: pinned to its current xprt (rebased from OE's 0x0040 — collides w/ RPC_TASK_NETUNREACH_FATAL on 7.0; needs widened tk_flags) */
+#endif
+
 #define RPC_IS_ASYNC(t)		((t)->tk_flags & RPC_TASK_ASYNC)
 #define RPC_IS_SWAPPER(t)	((t)->tk_flags & RPC_TASK_SWAPPER)
 #define RPC_IS_SOFT(t)		((t)->tk_flags & (RPC_TASK_SOFT|RPC_TASK_TIMEOUT))
